{
	title: 'command tool: the model runs slash commands',
	spec: 'The command tool runs slash commands in its own session through the same history, output and guard path as human commands. Commands are allowed by default. A denylist prevents /login, /quit, /suspend, /queue and /send. The model may read its spawn budget with bare /budget; any /budget argument from the model is refused, so only the user changes slots; /restart host|both|all is allowed so Hal can restart itself, and the tool description tells the model to run it only when the user asked or agreed, never on its own initiative; /queue and /send errors tell the model to use the send tool instead. Unknown commands and malformed input still fail. /auth is allowed, but its ephemeral code remains client-only output and never enters the tool result or history. /redraw repaints following terminals through a host event without restarting or reloading clients; typed terminal /redraw and Ctrl-L remain local. /fork, /branch, /new, /close, /resume, /pause, /config, /changes, /clients and /todo are allowed. Ordinary command guards remain in force. Hidden commands, including /branch, do not appear in terminal or web autocomplete; explicitly typing them still works. Remove tests of model command eligibility; add no new tests for this change.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'The model tool reuses slash.command, so it records the same command history and runs the same guards as typing a slash command. Eligibility is an explicit modelUsable registry flag, not inferred from server-side availability; slash.runCommand reports reply output/errors. Session-busy guards still prevent /clear and /compact while the model turn is active.',
		'The denylist replaces the earlier modelUsable registry flags. /redraw needs a host command and a transient redraw event because the original command ran only in terminals. The shared host completion path filters hidden entries for both clients.'
	],
	needs: [],
	foldInto: ['2t']
